comments[8]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-10-04T11:45:54.908Z","harness:codex","Duplicate check: complete live all-status corpus returned 2873 of 2873 records with zero omissions. Exact GH-1390 and issue URL were absent. Full relevant terminal predecessor metadata and comments were inspected. Request-specific search and open/in-progress inventories were refreshed. This distinct reported boundary is retained under the existing lineage and remains open and unclaimed."
  "2026-10-07T05:02:53.256Z","harness:codex","Delivery scope: authoritative receipt lifecycle composition, shared-worktree drift attribution and idempotent reconciliation, implemented alongside pm-gh1405. TDD owner: real shared Git worktrees and persisted history/receipt bytes; retain malformed/mismatched proof rejection. Full all-status duplicate check is complete at 2901 records; no new umbrella or duplicate item. Only the two actively edited owners are in_progress."
  "2026-10-07T05:08:47.421Z","harness:codex","TDD red evidence: real linked Git worktree with durable-only lossless receipt has merge_receipt_attributed_items empty and generic history repair guidance. Regression also asserts committed settlement dominates stale local pending bytes and a second SDK reconciliation leaves history and both receipt copies byte-identical. Immutable provenance validation remains mandatory."
  "2026-10-07T05:10:59.902Z","harness:codex","Additional TDD red: actual EACCES on durable receipt persistence occurs after the applied merge history audit commits. Retry appended a duplicate empty merge_reconcile event. The shared worktree keeper now requires byte-identical history across retry; the repair planner reuses only identical trusted receipt context, preserving force behavior and ordinary explicit audits."
  "2026-10-07T05:28:04.886Z","harness:codex","Repository context verification: full live health and history-drift validation pass. Health retains 14 advisory legacy hierarchy findings; validation reports 170 historical resolution-field warnings rather than integrity failures. Complete all-status intake and graph census include terminal history; no fabricated depth or inferred closure evidence is added. GitHub has no open PRs before this delivery, all 23 open issues have PM-file comments, and native security alert inventories plus dependency audit are empty. These observations do not claim the wider open roadmap complete."
  "2026-10-07T06:08:02.591Z","harness:codex","Final canonical runner passes 9,884 applicable tests with two Windows-only platform skips and exact all-source 100/100/100/100 coverage. Four TypeScript projects passed. Packed npx/bunx smoke passes all nine bundled packages; independent installed Node/Bun recovery journeys pass. The staged secret scan identified one machine-specific npm path in delivery evidence, now removed through verified history-redact plus a normal comment correction; item/history integrity remains valid and the staged scan passes. Final static validation and hosted review remain pending."
  "2026-10-07T06:36:27.909Z","harness:codex","PR 1422 first reviewed source head 5d198b93d054ecbe2e73b159fcaa8eb312479218 passes every one of the 26 effective required contexts; GitHub reports CLEAN with no missing checks. Native Windows recovery, coverage, static/type checks, CodeQL, Trivy, ShellCheck, PSScriptAnalyzer, actionlint, CodeFactor, DeepScan and package/runtime matrices pass. Review inventory has no inline findings: CodeRabbit automatic review skipped due repository star policy and must be explicitly triggered; Greptile trial ended and Sourcery review quota is exhausted. These provider limitations are not clean code-review approvals. Every current bot artifact will receive a usefulness vote and a specific linked acknowledgement before the final metadata push/retrigger."
  "2026-10-07T06:40:51.695Z","harness:codex","First feedback round completed: all six bot artifacts were read in full, voted thumbs-up for useful scope/coverage/availability information, and given specific artifact-linked revision-aware acknowledgements; there were no inline threads. Sourcery guide and benchmark report are contextual evidence; trial/quota notices remain limitations. CodeRabbit full manual review is requested after the final PM correction push, together with the other configured providers. Production source, test inputs and all-source coverage denominator are unchanged from the green reviewed source head."
notes[2]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-10-07T06:36:28.460Z","harness:codex","External DeepScan main dashboard inspected in Chrome: zero open issues at historical main analysis 686e7640a6455b65dbe9de82039a48c304598751, with an embedded ESLint integration warning. That old dashboard is not current-head evidence. The PR separately passes required native ESLint/static gates and exact-head DeepScan/CodeFactor contexts; confirm the final PR report before merge."
  "2026-10-07T06:40:51.066Z","harness:codex","Chrome verification of PR 1422: DeepScan explicitly shows source head 5d198b93d054ecbe2e73b159fcaa8eb312479218 with 0 new and 0 fixed issues; CodeFactor PR report says No issues found. Its main dashboard separately retains two duplicate reports for generated standalone plugin scripts and canonical templates. Existing .codefactor.yml identifies these generated mirrors as the hosted Ignore Files checklist, and generation/replication gates remain mandatory. Do not describe a green no-new-issues PR check as zero total baseline findings; retain that baseline under the existing quality lineage pm-92if without inventing another duplicate owner."
learnings[1]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-10-07T05:11:35.433Z","harness:codex","Committed durable lifecycle state must dominate stale worktree-local indexes only after exact immutable provenance validation. Retrying a history-committed, receipt-write-interrupted settlement must reuse its identical trusted audit context, while changed item proof and unrelated audits remain separate."
